output.generality:
Helps any hash join with exactly one equality key plus extra non-equality conditions (`!=`, `<`, `>`) when the build side is smaller than the probe side. Rewritten correlated EXISTS / NOT EXISTS subqueries with extra predicates are the common case. It also helps decorrelated subqueries whose build side is a DELIM_GET (the distinct outer keys), even when the probe-side scan has no filter of its own.

It does not apply to:
- joins with two or more equality keys (the filter API is single-column);
- a single NOT DISTINCT FROM equality;
- perfect hash joins;
- probe-side columns that need a cast.

When the filter rejects little, the existing SelectivityOptionalFilter switches it off at runtime. The cost is building the bloom filter on the build side.

